{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This backend supports Linux, macOS and Windows (maybe?), but its support for non-Linux platforms is significantly worse than "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/GtkBackend"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s (due to underlying Gtk 3 issues). Even on Linux, it’s recommended to use "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/GtkBackend"},{"type":"text","text":" over Gtk3Backend where possible."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Warning","style":"warning","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Non-Linux Gtk3Backend support is not a priority of this backend, and should only be used during development (e.g. to test your Linux UI natively on a Mac). There are multiple better choices of backend available on each non-Linux platform.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"},{"level":2,"anchor":"System-dependencies","text":"System dependencies","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Before you can use Gtk3Backend you must install the required system dependencies for your platform."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Linux","text":"Linux","type":"heading"},{"syntax":"sh","type":"codeListing","code":["sudo apt install libgtk-3-dev"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Figure 1: "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"installing Gtk 3 dev on an apt-based Linux distro"}]}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you are on a non-apt distro and the Gtk3Backend requirements end up differing significantly from the requirements stated above, please open a GitHub issue or PR so that we can improve the documentation."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"macOS","text":"macOS","type":"heading"},{"syntax":"sh","type":"codeListing","code":["brew install pkg-config gtk+3"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Figure 2: ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"installing Gtk 3 using Homebrew"}],"type":"emphasis"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you don’t have Homebrew, installation instructions can be found at "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/brew.sh"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It should also be possible to use ","type":"text"},{"code":"gtk3","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" installed via MacPorts, but I have not tested that.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Windows","text":"Windows","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"gtk3"},{"text":" installation has not been tested on Windows, and neither has Gtk3Backend, although there shouldn’t be anything to stop it from working (🤞). Follow the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"gtk4"},{"text":" installation instructions from ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/GtkBackend","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and replace ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"gtk"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"gtk3"},{"text":" in any vcpkg commands or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vcpkg.json"},{"text":" manifest files.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If you try this on Windows open a GitHub issue (even if it works without changes) so that we can fix any issues you faced and update this documentation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Usage","text":"Usage","type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["...","","let package = Package(","  ...","  targets: [","    ...","    .executableTarget(","      name: \"YourApp\",","      dependencies: [","        .product(name: \"SwiftCrossUI\", package: \"swift-cross-ui\"),","        .product(name: \"GtkBackend\", package: \"swift-cross-ui\"),","      ]","    )","    ...","  ]","  ...",")"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Figure 3: "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"adding "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Gtk3Backend"},{"type":"text","text":" to an executable target"}],"type":"emphasis"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiftCrossUI","import Gtk3Backend","","@main","struct YourApp: App {","  \/\/ You can explicitly initialize your app's chosen backend if you desire.","  \/\/ This happens automatically when you import any of the built-in backends.","  \/\/","  \/\/ var backend = Gtk3Backend()","  \/\/","  \/\/ If you aren't using Swift Bundler, you may have to explicitly provide","  \/\/ your app's identifier for some Gtk3Backend features to work correctly","  \/\/ (such as handling custom URL schemes).","  \/\/","  \/\/ var backend = Gtk3Backend(appIdentifier: \"com.example.YourApp\")","","  var body: some Scene {","    WindowGroup {","      Text(\"Hello, World!\")","        .padding()","    }","  }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Figure 4: "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"using "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Gtk3Backend"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/Gtk3Backend","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftcrossui\/gtk3backend"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Gtk3Backend","modules":[{"name":"SwiftCrossUI"}],"role":"article"},"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI","doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/Built-in-backends"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A secondary Linux backend built on top of Gtk 3 (for older distros without Gtk 4)."}],"seeAlsoSectio